cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Mimic, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Mimic: Efficient Human Mimicry"
abstract: >-
  Mimic learns a person from a short, adaptive Q&A session and persists a mimic that predicts their decisions.
  It is also a research platform for comparing cheap LLMs against a decision model at that task, with sealed,
  prequential predictions and a context-only baseline on every question.
authors:
  - family-names: Arani
    given-names: Punit
repository-code: "https://github.com/punitarani/mimic"
keywords:
  - digital twins
  - human decision prediction
  - adaptive questioning
  - LLM evaluation
